---
# P1-5 phase 2: static analysis via clang-tidy.
# Report-oriented, NON-BLOCKING: WarningsAsErrors is empty so findings are
# surfaced in CI logs but never fail a build or gate a merge.
#
# Scope is deliberately the plan's intended subset (bugprone-* + clang-analyzer-*)
# so it does not explode on pre-existing code. Two notoriously noisy
# bugprone-* checks are excluded:
#   -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters : flags any multi-param function of
#       same-adjacent-type, which floods every existing control/API signature.
#   -bugprone-narrowing-conversions      : reports implicit int/float narrowing
#       all over the existing GDI/Win32 layer; out of scope for this phase.
#
# FormatStyle: file  -> the format-style part of clang-tidy uses .clang-format.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: ''
FormatStyle: file